cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "EXAI-ResumeIntel: An Explainable Artificial Intelligence Framework for Automated Resume Analysis Using Shapley Values, LIME, and Domain Skill Ontology"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-01-15
authors:
  - family-names: "Sagar S"
    given-names: "Mithin"
    affiliation: "Vellore Institute of Technology (VIT)"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mithinsagar/EXAI-ResumeIntel"
url: "https://github.com/mithinsagar/EXAI-ResumeIntel"
abstract: >
  EXAI-ResumeIntel is a five-layer explainable AI framework for automated
  resume analysis. It combines a hierarchical domain skill ontology
  (22 canonical skills, 346 aliases), a custom TF-IDF + Truncated SVD
  semantic embedding engine, a four-component scoring model, and an XAI
  layer producing exact Shapley values, LIME local explanations,
  counterfactual scenarios, attention heatmaps, and natural language
  insights. Evaluated on 2,484 real-world resumes across 24 job categories
  using LinearSVC with 5-fold stratified cross-validation, the system
  achieves 70.73% overall accuracy and ROC-AUC scores ranging from 0.931
  to 0.993.
keywords:
  - explainable-ai
  - resume-analysis
  - shapley-values
  - lime
